  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida has $24.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 167,062 contracts in the state, with an average award size of $149K. Obligations are down 23.1% year over year. The fiscal picture for the state shows a lower current-year total compared with recent full fiscal years, and the Department of Defense is the single largest buyer in this period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date records $24.9B in obligations, below the prior-year total of $32.5B in FY25. Obligations rose through FY21 to FY25, peaking at $32.5B in FY25 before the FY2026 to date decline. Obligations are down 23.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drive federal spending in Florida?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $17B in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $2.6B and the General Services Administration with $1.6B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry with $4.6B, and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction follows with $2.3B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Florida?",
      "a": "Florida has received $24.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 167,062 contracts in the state, and the average award size is $149K."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Florida?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $17B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2.6B, and the General Services Administration obligated $1.6B; other top buyers include the Department of Homeland Security with $1.2B and NASA with $676M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Florida?",
      "a": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the largest vendor with $2.6B in obligations. Other top vendors include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION again with $2.3B, THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC with $1.9B, and LOYAL SOURCE GOVERNMENT SERVICES LLC with $1.8B."
